<title>DENMARK: Danish August trade surplus 2.839 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish August trade surplus 2.839 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 2.839 billion crowns in August 1996 compared to a revised 1.770 billion crowns in July 1996, the national statistics office said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     August 1996    July 1996  August 1995</p>
<p> Exports			 22.871	  20.790	22.745</p>
<p> Imports			 19.819	  18.462	19.616</p>
<p> Trade balance		  3.052	   2.329	 3.129</p>
<p> Trade balance excl ships   2.839	   1.770	 3.137</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	  2.763	   3.052	 3.019</p>
<p>balance excluding ships</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average August surplus excluding ships of 2.5 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
